# CODEOWNERS — who is asked to review changes to which part of this repository.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS: replace every `@<org>/<team-…>` with a real GitHub team when you
# start a project from this starter. Two things to know:
#   * An owner GitHub cannot resolve (placeholder, typo, missing team) is skipped
#     without any warning, so until real teams are filled in nothing is requested.
#   * Review is only *required* once branch protection on `dev` and `main` has
#     "Require review from Code Owners" turned on.
#
# Last match wins, so the catch-all comes first and specific paths below it.

*                                   @<org>/<team-leads>

# Applications — one deployable each.
/apps/web/                          @<org>/<team-frontend>
/apps/api/                          @<org>/<team-backend>

# Shared packages — a change here affects every consuming app.
/packages/                          @<org>/<team-backend> @<org>/<team-frontend>

# Database schema. Migrations reach prod through CI, so review here IS the gate.
/tools/supabase/                    @<org>/<team-backend> @<org>/<team-platform>

# Infrastructure and the pipelines that apply it. Changes here change who can
# reach which AWS account (OIDC trust policies) — keep this list short.
/tools/infra/                       @<org>/<team-platform>
/.github/                           @<org>/<team-platform>
/CODEOWNERS                         @<org>/<team-platform>

# Agent instructions and the rules about the rules.
/AGENTS.md                          @<org>/<team-leads>
/CLAUDE.md                          @<org>/<team-leads>
/docs/                              @<org>/<team-leads>
